on between "modest, functional trait tendencies" (fine to state) and "sweeping, judgmental characterizations of most people in a huge, varied group" (need real evidence, not vibes and repetition). That's not an absurd place to land — it's basically just... normal epistemic caution, applied consistently rather than only when it's convenient.
